VERDICT: REVISE
BLOCKERS: (1) run_recorder.record_lifecycle_projection_diff computes `differences` purely from ledger events/state (missing_question_admission, revision_id mismatch, missing_evidence_for_run) but never compares legacy `spec.get("status")` against projection execution outcome — a real drift between legacy execution status and lifecycle-projected state would silently record zero differences, so "30 consecutive zero-diff cycles" can be satisfied while lifecycle projection and legacy status actually disagree; this is exactly the fabricated-zero-diff risk the gate is meant to catch. (2) `compile_proxy`/spec_compiler path stamps `proposal["research_lifecycle"]` before compile_outcome is known and `_base_spec` copies it into `spec["research_lifecycle"]` unconditionally regardless of compile result (DRAFT vs READY), yet `record_revision` is only called after compile in the ideation cycle — verify DRAFT (failed) revisions still get `record_revision` called with `compile_outcome=result.status` (they do, per code shown), but the test `test_revision_compile_outcome_controls_executability_projection` only checks state transitions, not that repeated same-question DRAFT→DRAFT calls with new proposal_ids don't double-count against revision_budget when compile fails — no test asserts budget doesn't leak on failed compiles. (3) `record_lifecycle_evidence`/`record_lifecycle_projection_diff` treat `spec.status` implicitly as authoritative for compare's "legacy" block (`"legacy": {"execution_status": spec.get("status"), ...}`) with no validation that this legacy status is itself derived correctly (e.g. via `status_for_decision`) — if spec.status is stale or hand-set, compare silently accepts it as ground truth. (4) Evidence-append dedup in `record_lifecycle_projection_diff` keys solely on `run_id`, so a legitimate re-run reusing an old run_id (or backfill) would be silently dropped rather than flagged, risking missed evidence without any warning/error path.
TESTS: Present but insufficient — idempotency and 30/consecutive-window logic covered (using minimum_cycles=2 as proxy), but no test exercises a genuine legacy-vs-projection status disagreement to confirm `differences` catches it, and no test covers DRAFT-compile revision budget accounting across repeated failed compiles.
